abstract: >-
  Freefield is an intuitive tool to design and conduct
  psychoacoustic experiments with Tucker-Davis Technologies
  (TDT) Hardware in Python. Freefield was originally
  developed for the anechoic chamber at the University of
  Leipzig. It has since been generalized to support custom
  experimental setups. Now it allows you to easily create
  your own unique experiment setups and let freefield handle
  essential operations like writing to and reading from
  buffers, recording signals or creating loudspeaker
  equalization for you.
